Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: keel-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: OpenPGP public keys of the Keel Linux signing roles
 The public keys that sign what Keel Linux publishes, one key for each
 role, each in its own keyring file for the Signed-By field of an apt
 source:
  * main, the trixie suite: /usr/share/keyrings/keel-archive-keyring.gpg
  * security, the trixie-security suite: keel-security-keyring.gpg
  * testing, the trixie-testing suite: keel-testing-keyring.gpg
  * images, the release images and the Proxmox index:
    keel-images-keyring.gpg
 .
 The keys are never merged into one keyring, so a key of one role cannot
 sign for another role. The fingerprint of the main primary key is in
 /usr/share/keel-archive-keyring/fingerprint, and the fingerprints of all
 roles are in /usr/share/keel-archive-keyring/FINGERPRINTS.
 .
 The package installs the keys and nothing else. It does not add an apt
 source, does not change the configuration of apt and has no maintainer
 script.
